{
  "type": "74hc193",
  "name": "74HC193 4-bit up/down counter",
  "category": "Logic chips (DIP)",
  "prefix": "U",
  "description": "Presettable up/down counter (DIP-16): counts up at the rising edge of CPU while CPD is high and down at the rising edge of CPD while CPU is high; PL low loads D0-D3 and MR high clears it, at once; TCU and TCD go low at 15 (CPU low) and at 0 (CPD low) for cascading; runs as a digital chip: with a board or on its own, inputs from the rest of the circuit arrive up to 0.1 ms late (clocks up to a few kHz)",
